Step 2 details
  - core/interfaces.py: SequenceMixer, FeedForward, TokenMemory, Residual, OutputHead
    (runtime_checkable Protocols) + MixerCaps (frozen). Every sublayer returns
    (update [T,D], AuxOutputs).
  - core/registry.py: Registry + MIXERS, FFNS, RESIDUALS, TOKEN_MEMORIES, OUTPUT_HEADS.
    model/components.py imports all implementation modules so they register.
  - Constructors: mixers/FFNs/memories (config, layer_idx); residual (config);
    head (config, embedding).
  - Registered now: MIXERS "gqa", FFNS "moe", RESIDUALS "standard", OUTPUT_HEADS "lm".
  - ModelConfig: LayerSpec(mixer, ffn, memory=None); layers defaults to num_layers copies;
    residual="standard"; output_head="lm".
  - Generic block: residual.read -> norm -> mixer -> residual.write -> norm -> ffn -> write.
    Residual lives at model level; write never in place.
  - LM head owns the final norm.
  - MixerCaps: set a flag only once a contract test proves it (GQA: needs_positions only).
  - Router bias update moves from forward to FeedForward.post_step();
    TransformerLM.post_step() called by the trainer once per optimizer step.
  - Checkpoint keys renamed (attention->mixer, attn_norm->mixer_norm, moe->ffn,
    moe_norm->ffn_norm, final_norm->head.norm, lm_head->head.proj);
    model/checkpoint_migration.py::migrate_state_dict, applied in generate_setup.
  - Tests: tests/test_model_contracts.py (+ golden + existing suite stay green).
  Checks to watch for:
  - LM head ties by sharing the Parameter, not by storing the embedding module
    (a stored module adds a head.embedding.weight key that old checkpoints lack).
  - Keep parameter registration order (norm, mixer, norm, ffn; head.norm then head.proj),
    so saved optimizer state still lines up with parameters on resume.
  - Routing statistics: accumulate expert counts (not fractions) in training forwards only;
    the accumulators are non-persistent buffers, reset in post_step.
  - ModelConfig with LayerSpec must still save to JSON (checkpoint.py dumps __dict__).
  - migrate_state_dict also needed when resuming training (training/checkpoint.py), not just generate_setup.


